{"type":"data","nodes":[{"type":"data","data":[{"docsStarts":1},{"foundation":2,"assurance":3},"/foundation/docs/","/assurance/docs/getting-started/"],"uses":{}},null,{"type":"data","data":[{"docs":1,"source":16},{"nav":2,"slugs":15,"first":6},[3,7,11],{"name":4,"href":5,"slug":6},"Guide","/foundation/docs/","index",{"name":8,"href":9,"slug":10},"Analyzers","/foundation/docs/analyzers/","analyzers",{"name":12,"href":13,"slug":14},"Performance","/foundation/docs/performance/","performance",[6,10,14],{"repo":17,"version":18},"https://github.com/AHRConsulting/Ahr.Foundation","0.2.0"],"uses":{"params":["product"]}},{"type":"data","data":[{"slug":1,"page":2},"analyzers",{"slug":1,"title":3,"html":4,"headings":5,"source":31},"Roslyn Analyzers","\u003Cp>The \u003Ccode>Ahr.Foundation\u003C/code> NuGet package includes \u003Ccode>Ahr.Foundation.Analyzers\u003C/code>. The .NET SDK loads the\nanalyzer assembly automatically from the package's \u003Ccode>analyzers/dotnet/cs\u003C/code> directory, so consumers\ndo not need to install or configure a second package. The analyzer is a build-time development\nasset and does not add a runtime dependency.\u003C/p>\n\u003Cp>The analyzers load in any C# compiler from Roslyn 4.0 onward: the .NET 6 SDK or newer, and\nVisual Studio 2022 17.0 or newer. An older compiler still builds the project and uses the library;\nit reports \u003Ccode>CS9057\u003C/code> or \u003Ccode>CS8032\u003C/code> and skips only the analyzers.\u003C/p>\n\u003Ch2 id=\"rules\">Rules\u003C/h2>\n\u003Cdiv class=\"table-wrap\">\u003Ctable>\n\u003Cthead>\n\u003Ctr>\n\u003Cth>Rule\u003C/th>\n\u003Cth>Severity\u003C/th>\n\u003Cth>Description\u003C/th>\n\u003C/tr>\n\u003C/thead>\n\u003Ctbody>\n\u003Ctr>\n\u003Ctd>\u003Ccode>AHRF001\u003C/code>\u003C/td>\n\u003Ctd>Error\u003C/td>\n\u003Ctd>Result values must be created explicitly rather than with \u003Ccode>default\u003C/code> or parameterless construction.\u003C/td>\n\u003C/tr>\n\u003Ctr>\n\u003Ctd>\u003Ccode>AHRF002\u003C/code>\u003C/td>\n\u003Ctd>Info\u003C/td>\n\u003Ctd>Prefer \u003Ccode>Result.Try\u003C/code> or \u003Ccode>Result.TryAsync\u003C/code> when a manual try/catch only converts success and failure into a \u003Ccode>Result\u003C/code>.\u003C/td>\n\u003C/tr>\n\u003Ctr>\n\u003Ctd>\u003Ccode>AHRF003\u003C/code>\u003C/td>\n\u003Ctd>Warning\u003C/td>\n\u003Ctd>Use \u003Ccode>Result.TryAsync\u003C/code> when the operation returns \u003Ccode>Task\u003C/code>, \u003Ccode>Task&lt;T&gt;\u003C/code>, \u003Ccode>ValueTask\u003C/code>, or \u003Ccode>ValueTask&lt;T&gt;\u003C/code>.\u003C/td>\n\u003C/tr>\n\u003Ctr>\n\u003Ctd>\u003Ccode>AHRF004\u003C/code>\u003C/td>\n\u003Ctd>Warning\u003C/td>\n\u003Ctd>Do not pass an async delegate typed or cast as \u003Ccode>Action\u003C/code> to \u003Ccode>Result.Try\u003C/code>; post-await exceptions cannot be captured.\u003C/td>\n\u003C/tr>\n\u003Ctr>\n\u003Ctd>\u003Ccode>AHRF005\u003C/code>\u003C/td>\n\u003Ctd>Info\u003C/td>\n\u003Ctd>Elements of a Result array created without initializers start uninitialized and must each be assigned before use.\u003C/td>\n\u003C/tr>\n\u003Ctr>\n\u003Ctd>\u003Ccode>AHRF006\u003C/code>\u003C/td>\n\u003Ctd>Warning\u003C/td>\n\u003Ctd>\u003Ccode>Map\u003C/code>, \u003Ccode>MapAsync\u003C/code>, \u003Ccode>MapSome\u003C/code>, \u003Ccode>MapSomeAsync\u003C/code>, \u003Ccode>Select\u003C/code>, \u003Ccode>Try\u003C/code>, and \u003Ccode>TryAsync\u003C/code> must not produce a nullable value; a null result throws. Use \u003Ccode>Bind\u003C/code>, or return an \u003Ccode>Option\u003C/code> from the operation.\u003C/td>\n\u003C/tr>\n\u003Ctr>\n\u003Ctd>\u003Ccode>AHRF007\u003C/code>\u003C/td>\n\u003Ctd>Info\u003C/td>\n\u003Ctd>A \u003Ccode>Result.TryAsync\u003C/code> operation uses a caller's cancellation token; pass it to the overload that takes a \u003Ccode>CancellationToken\u003C/code>.\u003C/td>\n\u003C/tr>\n\u003Ctr>\n\u003Ctd>\u003Ccode>AHRF008\u003C/code>\u003C/td>\n\u003Ctd>Warning\u003C/td>\n\u003Ctd>A \u003Ccode>Tap\u003C/code>, \u003Ccode>TapAsync\u003C/code>, \u003Ccode>TapSome\u003C/code>, or \u003Ccode>TapSomeAsync\u003C/code> function discards a result or option, so a failure is ignored.\u003C/td>\n\u003C/tr>\n\u003Ctr>\n\u003Ctd>\u003Ccode>AHRF009\u003C/code>\u003C/td>\n\u003Ctd>Info\u003C/td>\n\u003Ctd>\u003Ccode>GetValueOrDefault\u003C/code> or \u003Ccode>ToOption\u003C/code> on a result of an option discards the failure; use the three-way \u003Ccode>Match\u003C/code>, \u003Ccode>SomeOr\u003C/code>, or \u003Ccode>EnsureSome\u003C/code>.\u003C/td>\n\u003C/tr>\n\u003Ctr>\n\u003Ctd>\u003Ccode>AHRF010\u003C/code>\u003C/td>\n\u003Ctd>Warning\u003C/td>\n\u003Ctd>A statement discards a \u003Ccode>Result\u003C/code>, or a \u003Ccode>Task\u003C/code> or \u003Ccode>ValueTask\u003C/code> of one, so a failure is lost.\u003C/td>\n\u003C/tr>\n\u003Ctr>\n\u003Ctd>\u003Ccode>AHRF011\u003C/code>\u003C/td>\n\u003Ctd>Info\u003C/td>\n\u003Ctd>A failure is passed on unchanged by hand; use \u003Ccode>Bind\u003C/code> or \u003Ccode>BindAsync\u003C/code>.\u003C/td>\n\u003C/tr>\n\u003C/tbody>\n\u003C/table>\u003C/div>\n\u003Cp>All rules are enabled by default.\u003C/p>\n\u003Ch2 id=\"explicit-result-construction\">Explicit Result Construction\u003C/h2>\n\u003Cp>\u003Ccode>Result\u003C/code>, \u003Ccode>Result&lt;T&gt;\u003C/code>, and \u003Ccode>Result&lt;T, TError&gt;\u003C/code> have an uninitialized default state. \u003Ccode>AHRF001\u003C/code>\nreports detectable default construction before that value can reach runtime:\u003C/p>\n\u003Cpre class=\"code\" data-lang=\"csharp\">\u003Ccode>\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-type)\">Result\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\"> invalid \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-keyword)\">=\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-keyword)\"> default\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">;       \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-comment)\">// AHRF001\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-type)\">Result\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\"> valid \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-keyword)\">=\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\"> Result.\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-function)\">Success\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">();\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\u003C/code>\u003C/pre>\n\u003Cp>The supplied code fix can replace a default-constructed payload-free \u003Ccode>Result\u003C/code> with\n\u003Ccode>Result.Success()\u003C/code>. Generic results require choosing an intentional success value or failure:\u003C/p>\n\u003Cpre class=\"code\" data-lang=\"csharp\">\u003Ccode>\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-type)\">Result\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">&#x3C;\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-type)\">User\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">> user \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-keyword)\">=\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\"> Result&#x3C;\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-type)\">User\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">>.\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-function)\">Failure\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">(\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-keyword)\">new\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-type)\"> Error\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">(\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-string)\">\"User was not loaded.\"\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">));\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\u003C/code>\u003C/pre>\n\u003Cp>Arrays are reported separately. A Result array created without element initializers is a common\nallocate-then-fill pattern, so \u003Ccode>AHRF005\u003C/code> reports it at Info severity rather than failing the build:\u003C/p>\n\u003Cpre class=\"code\" data-lang=\"csharp\">\u003Ccode>\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-keyword)\">var\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\"> results \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-keyword)\">=\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-keyword)\"> new\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-type)\"> Result\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">&#x3C;\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-type)\">Order\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">>[ids.Length]; \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-comment)\">// AHRF005: assign every element before use\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-keyword)\">for\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\"> (\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-keyword)\">var\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\"> i \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-keyword)\">=\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-number)\"> 0\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">; i \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-keyword)\">&#x3C;\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\"> ids.Length; i\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-keyword)\">++\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">)\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">{\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">    results[i] \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-keyword)\">=\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-function)\"> LoadOrder\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">(ids[i]);\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">}\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\u003C/code>\u003C/pre>\n\u003Cp>\u003Ccode>Option&lt;T&gt;\u003C/code> is intentionally different: its default value safely represents \u003Ccode>None\u003C/code>, so\nneither \u003Ccode>AHRF001\u003C/code> nor \u003Ccode>AHRF005\u003C/code> reports default option construction.\u003C/p>\n\u003Ch2 id=\"mapping-to-nullable-values\">Mapping to Nullable Values\u003C/h2>\n\u003Cp>\u003Ccode>Some\u003C/code> and \u003Ccode>Success\u003C/code> never hold \u003Ccode>null\u003C/code>, so \u003Ccode>Map\u003C/code>, \u003Ccode>MapAsync\u003C/code>, \u003Ccode>MapSome\u003C/code>, \u003Ccode>MapSomeAsync\u003C/code>, and \u003Ccode>Select\u003C/code>\nthrow \u003Ccode>ArgumentNullException\u003C/code> when the mapping returns \u003Ccode>null\u003C/code>. \u003Ccode>AHRF006\u003C/code> reports a mapping whose result\ntype is nullable, such as \u003Ccode>string?\u003C/code> or \u003Ccode>int?\u003C/code>, so the mistake appears at compile time instead:\u003C/p>\n\u003Cpre class=\"code\" data-lang=\"csharp\">\u003Ccode>\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-type)\">Option\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">&#x3C;\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-keyword)\">string\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">> middle \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-keyword)\">=\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\"> customer.\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-function)\">Map\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">(c \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-keyword)\">=>\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\"> c.MiddleName);            \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-comment)\">// AHRF006\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-type)\">Option\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">&#x3C;\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-keyword)\">string\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">> middle \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-keyword)\">=\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\"> customer.\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-function)\">Bind\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">(c \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-keyword)\">=>\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\"> c.MiddleName.\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-function)\">ToOption\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">()); \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-comment)\">// null becomes None\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-type)\">Result\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">&#x3C;\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-keyword)\">string\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">> city \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-keyword)\">=\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\"> order.\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-function)\">Map\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">(o \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-keyword)\">=>\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\"> o.Address.City);               \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-comment)\">// AHRF006\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-type)\">Result\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">&#x3C;\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-keyword)\">string\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">> city \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-keyword)\">=\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\"> order.\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-function)\">Bind\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">(o \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-keyword)\">=>\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\"> o.Address.City \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-keyword)\">is\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\"> { } value\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-keyword)\">    ?\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\"> Result&#x3C;\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-keyword)\">string\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">>.\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-function)\">Success\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">(value)\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-keyword)\">    :\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\"> Result&#x3C;\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-keyword)\">string\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">>.\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-function)\">Failure\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">(\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-keyword)\">new\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-type)\"> Error\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">(\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-string)\">\"The order has no delivery city.\"\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">)));\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\u003C/code>\u003C/pre>\n\u003Cp>The rule relies on nullable annotations, so it reports only in a nullable-enabled context. LINQ\nquery syntax (\u003Ccode>select c.MiddleName\u003C/code>) is not reported because the compiler does not track\nnullability through query expressions. A mapping declared non-nullable that still returns \u003Ccode>null\u003C/code>\nat runtime continues to throw.\u003C/p>\n\u003Cp>\u003Ccode>Result.Try\u003C/code> and \u003Ccode>Result.TryAsync\u003C/code> follow the same rule: an operation declared to return a nullable\ntype is reported, because a \u003Ccode>null\u003C/code> success throws. Return an \u003Ccode>Option\u003C/code> from the operation instead:\u003C/p>\n\u003Cpre class=\"code\" data-lang=\"csharp\">\u003Ccode>\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-type)\">Result\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">&#x3C;\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-keyword)\">object\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">> shown \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-keyword)\">=\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-keyword)\"> await\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\"> Result.\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-function)\">TryAsync\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">(presenter.ShowAsync, ct);                    \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-comment)\">// AHRF006 when ShowAsync returns Task&#x3C;object?>\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-type)\">Result\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">&#x3C;\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-type)\">Option\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">&#x3C;\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-keyword)\">object\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">>> shown \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-keyword)\">=\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-keyword)\"> await\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\"> Result.\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-function)\">TryAsync\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">(\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-keyword)\">    async\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\"> token \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-keyword)\">=>\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\"> (\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-keyword)\">await\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\"> presenter.\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-function)\">ShowAsync\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">(token)).\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-function)\">ToOption\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">(), ct);                    \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-comment)\">// null becomes None\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\u003C/code>\u003C/pre>\n\u003Ch2 id=\"safe-exception-adapters\">Safe Exception Adapters\u003C/h2>\n\u003Cp>The remaining rules protect the boundary between exception-based APIs and result-based code:\u003C/p>\n\u003Cpre class=\"code\" data-lang=\"csharp\">\u003Ccode>\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-comment)\">// AHRF002: this shape can be replaced with Result.Try.\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-type)\">Result\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">&#x3C;\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-type)\">Order\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">> \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-function)\">LoadOrder\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">()\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">{\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-keyword)\">    try\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">    {\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-keyword)\">        return\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\"> Result&#x3C;\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-type)\">Order\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">>.\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-function)\">Success\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">(repository.\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-function)\">Load\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">());\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">    }\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-keyword)\">    catch\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\"> (\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-type)\">Exception\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\"> exception)\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">    {\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-keyword)\">        return\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\"> Result&#x3C;\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-type)\">Order\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">>.\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-function)\">Failure\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">(Error.\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-function)\">FromException\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">(exception));\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">    }\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">}\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-comment)\">// Not reported: Result.Try rethrows cancellation, so this catch cannot be replaced.\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-type)\">Result\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-function)\"> Save\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">(\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-type)\">CancellationToken\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\"> cancellationToken)\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">{\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-keyword)\">    try\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">    {\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">        repository.\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-function)\">Save\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">(cancellationToken);\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-keyword)\">        return\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\"> Result.\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-function)\">Success\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">();\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">    }\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-keyword)\">    catch\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\"> (\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-type)\">OperationCanceledException\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">)\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">    {\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-keyword)\">        return\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\"> Result.\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-function)\">Failure\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">(\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-keyword)\">new\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-type)\"> Error\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">(\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-string)\">\"Cancelled.\"\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">));\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">    }\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">}\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-comment)\">// AHRF002 also reports a try/catch/finally. Keep the cleanup around the call:\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-keyword)\">try\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">{\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-keyword)\">    return\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\"> Result.\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-function)\">Try\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">(() \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-keyword)\">=>\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\"> repository.\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-function)\">Load\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">());\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">}\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-keyword)\">finally\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">{\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">    gate.\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-function)\">Release\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">();\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">}\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-comment)\">// AHRF003: the asynchronous operation must be awaited by TryAsync.\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">_ \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-keyword)\">=\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\"> Result.\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-function)\">Try\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">(() \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-keyword)\">=>\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\"> repository.\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-function)\">LoadAsync\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">());\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-type)\">Result\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">&#x3C;\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-type)\">Order\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">> order \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-keyword)\">=\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-keyword)\"> await\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\"> Result.\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-function)\">TryAsync\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">(() \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-keyword)\">=>\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\"> repository.\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-function)\">LoadAsync\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">());\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\u003C/code>\u003C/pre>\n\u003Cp>\u003Ccode>AHRF004\u003C/code> covers the narrower async-void form, such as\n\u003Ccode>Result.Try((Action)(async () =&gt; await repository.SaveAsync()))\u003C/code>. Use \u003Ccode>Result.TryAsync\u003C/code> instead so\nthe operation is awaited and exceptions become a \u003Ccode>Failure\u003C/code>. The analyzer detects inline async\n\u003Ccode>Action\u003C/code> expressions, including explicit casts, but does not perform data-flow analysis to trace a\ndelegate variable back to the async lambda assigned to it.\u003C/p>\n\u003Ch2 id=\"cancellation-aware-tryasync\">Cancellation-Aware TryAsync\u003C/h2>\n\u003Cp>\u003Ccode>Result.TryAsync\u003C/code> overloads without a token propagate every \u003Ccode>OperationCanceledException\u003C/code>, including\ncancellations the caller never requested. \u003Ccode>HttpClient\u003C/code>, for example, reports a timeout as a\n\u003Ccode>TaskCanceledException\u003C/code>, so the timeout escapes instead of becoming a \u003Ccode>Failure\u003C/code>. The overloads that\ntake a \u003Ccode>CancellationToken\u003C/code> pass the token to the operation, propagate only that token's\ncancellation, and convert any other cancellation into a \u003Ccode>Failure\u003C/code>. A token that is already canceled\nthrows before the operation runs.\u003C/p>\n\u003Cp>\u003Ccode>AHRF007\u003C/code> reports a \u003Ccode>TryAsync\u003C/code> operation that uses a cancellation token from the surrounding code: a\nparameter, a local, or a member such as \u003Ccode>HttpContext.RequestAborted\u003C/code>. \u003Ccode>CancellationToken.None\u003C/code>,\n\u003Ccode>default\u003C/code>, and tokens created inside the operation are not reported.\u003C/p>\n\u003Cpre class=\"code\" data-lang=\"csharp\">\u003Ccode>\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-comment)\">// AHRF007: the operation uses 'cancellationToken'\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-type)\">Result\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">&#x3C;\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-keyword)\">string\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">> body \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-keyword)\">=\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-keyword)\"> await\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\"> Result.\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-function)\">TryAsync\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">(() \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-keyword)\">=>\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\"> client.\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-function)\">GetStringAsync\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">(url, cancellationToken));\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-comment)\">// After the code fix\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-type)\">Result\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">&#x3C;\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-keyword)\">string\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">> body \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-keyword)\">=\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-keyword)\"> await\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\"> Result.\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-function)\">TryAsync\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">(token \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-keyword)\">=>\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\"> client.\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-function)\">GetStringAsync\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">(url, token), cancellationToken);\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\u003C/code>\u003C/pre>\n\u003Cp>The rule reports at Info severity because the existing call is not wrong: it changes only how\ncancellations other than the caller's surface. Review code that catches \u003Ccode>TaskCanceledException\u003C/code>\naround the call before applying the fix. The code fix runs only when invoked, supports Fix All, and\nis not offered when the operation uses more than one distinct token.\u003C/p>\n\u003Ch2 id=\"discarded-results-in-tap\">Discarded Results in Tap\u003C/h2>\n\u003Cp>A \u003Ccode>Tap\u003C/code> function that returns the same family stops the pipeline on failure or \u003Ccode>None\u003C/code>. When the\nfunction discards the value instead, the failure goes unnoticed, so \u003Ccode>AHRF008\u003C/code> reports it:\u003C/p>\n\u003Cpre class=\"code\" data-lang=\"csharp\">\u003Ccode>\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-type)\">Result\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">&#x3C;\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-keyword)\">int\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">> result \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-keyword)\">=\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-function)\"> LoadTotal\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">();\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">_ \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-keyword)\">=\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\"> result.\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-function)\">Tap\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">(total \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-keyword)\">=>\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\"> { \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-function)\">Save\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">(total); });      \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-comment)\">// AHRF008: block body has no return\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">_ \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-keyword)\">=\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\"> option.\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-function)\">Tap\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">(value =\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-keyword)\">>\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-function)\"> Save\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">(value));           \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-comment)\">// AHRF008: an option cannot carry the failure\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">_ \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-keyword)\">=\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\"> customError.\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-function)\">Tap\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">(value =\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-keyword)\">>\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-function)\"> Save\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">(value));      \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-comment)\">// AHRF008: a different error type\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">_ \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-keyword)\">=\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\"> result.\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-function)\">Tap\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">(total \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-keyword)\">=>\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-function)\"> Save\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">(total));           \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-comment)\">// a failure stops the pipeline\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">_ \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-keyword)\">=\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\"> result.\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-function)\">Tap\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">(total \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-keyword)\">=>\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\"> { _ \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-keyword)\">=\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-function)\"> Save\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">(total); });  \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-comment)\">// ignored deliberately\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\u003C/code>\u003C/pre>\n\u003Cp>Return a value of the same family, convert it, or use \u003Ccode>Bind\u003C/code>. Assign the value to \u003Ccode>_\u003C/code> when ignoring it\nis intentional. \u003Ccode>TapSome\u003C/code> and \u003Ccode>TapSomeAsync\u003C/code> on \u003Ccode>Result&lt;Option&lt;T&gt;&gt;\u003C/code> are checked the same way.\n\u003Ccode>TapError\u003C/code> and nested lambdas are not analyzed.\u003C/p>\n\u003Ch2 id=\"discarded-results\">Discarded Results\u003C/h2>\n\u003Cp>A \u003Ccode>Result\u003C/code> is often the only signal that an operation failed. \u003Ccode>AHRF010\u003C/code> reports a statement that drops\none, including an awaited call, a call that is not awaited, and a statement in a lambda with no return\nvalue:\u003C/p>\n\u003Cpre class=\"code\" data-lang=\"csharp\">\u003Ccode>\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-function)\">Save\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">(order);                         \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-comment)\">// AHRF010\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-keyword)\">await\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-function)\"> SaveAsync\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">(order, ct);          \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-comment)\">// AHRF010: awaiting does not handle the failure\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-function)\">SaveAsync\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">(order, ct);                \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-comment)\">// AHRF010: not awaited\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-function)\">LoadOrder\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">(id).\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-function)\">Tap\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">(Use);              \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-comment)\">// AHRF010: Tap runs only on success\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-type)\">Action\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\"> save \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-keyword)\">=\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\"> () \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-keyword)\">=>\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-function)\"> Save\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">(order);     \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-comment)\">// AHRF010\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-type)\">Result\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\"> saved \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-keyword)\">=\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-function)\"> Save\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">(order);          \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-comment)\">// assigned\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-function)\">Save\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">(order).\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-function)\">TapError\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">(Log);           \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-comment)\">// the chain ends by handling the failure\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-keyword)\">await\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-function)\"> SaveAsync\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">(order, ct).\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-function)\">TapErrorAsync\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">(Log);\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">_ \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-keyword)\">=\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-function)\"> Save\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">(order);                     \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-comment)\">// ignored deliberately\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\u003C/code>\u003C/pre>\n\u003Cp>A \u003Ccode>Match\u003C/code> that takes actions handles the failure, so it is not reported, even though it returns the\nresult. A \u003Ccode>Match\u003C/code> whose functions return a result is reported. \u003Ccode>Option&lt;T&gt;\u003C/code> is not analyzed, because \u003Ccode>None\u003C/code> is not a\nfailure. A drop inside a \u003Ccode>Tap\u003C/code> function is reported by \u003Ccode>AHRF008\u003C/code> instead. The rule treats \u003Ccode>_ =\u003C/code> as a\ndecision, so review these assignments as you would any ignored error. A \u003Ccode>Task&lt;Result&gt;\u003C/code> converted to a\nplain \u003Ccode>Task\u003C/code>, such as \u003Ccode>Func&lt;Task&gt; save = () =&gt; SaveAsync(order, ct);\u003C/code>, is not detected.\u003C/p>\n\u003Cp>To allow discards in a project such as a test project, lower the severity in \u003Ccode>.editorconfig\u003C/code>:\u003C/p>\n\u003Cpre class=\"code\" data-lang=\"text\">\u003Ccode>\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan>[tests/**.cs]\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan>dotnet_diagnostic.AHRF010.severity = none\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\u003C/code>\u003C/pre>\n\u003Ch2 id=\"failures-passed-on-by-hand\">Failures Passed On by Hand\u003C/h2>\n\u003Cp>\u003Ccode>AHRF011\u003C/code> reports a check that returns the failure unchanged, which is what \u003Ccode>Bind\u003C/code> and \u003Ccode>BindAsync\u003C/code> do:\u003C/p>\n\u003Cpre class=\"code\" data-lang=\"csharp\">\u003Ccode>\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-keyword)\">return\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\"> loaded.IsFailure \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-keyword)\">?\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\"> Result&#x3C;\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-type)\">Page\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">>.\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-function)\">Failure\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">(loaded.Error) \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-keyword)\">:\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-function)\"> Build\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">(loaded.Value);  \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-comment)\">// AHRF011\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-keyword)\">return\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\"> loaded.\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-function)\">Bind\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">(value =\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-keyword)\">>\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-function)\"> Build\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">(value));                                           \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-comment)\">// after the code fix\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-keyword)\">if\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\"> (loaded.IsFailure)                                                                \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-comment)\">// AHRF011\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">{\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-keyword)\">    return\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\"> Result&#x3C;\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-type)\">Page\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">>.\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-function)\">Failure\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">(loaded.Error);\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\n\u003Cspan class=\"line\">\u003Cspan style=\"color:var(--ahr-code-fg)\">}\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\u003C/code>\u003C/pre>\n\u003Cp>A failure wrapped in \u003Ccode>Task.FromResult\u003C/code> or \u003Ccode>ValueTask.FromResult\u003C/code>, in a method that returns a task\nwithout being \u003Ccode>async\u003C/code>, is reported too; \u003Ccode>BindAsync\u003C/code> replaces it.\u003C/p>\n\u003Cp>The code fix rewrites the conditional expression to \u003Ccode>Bind\u003C/code>, except when the failure is wrapped in a\ntask. An early return has no automatic fix,\nbecause the rest of the method would move into the \u003Ccode>Bind\u003C/code> function. A failure that is changed, logged,\nor combined with another result is not reported, nor is a check inside a loop or a \u003Ccode>try\u003C/code>, \u003Ccode>using\u003C/code>, or\n\u003Ccode>lock\u003C/code> block. The failure must keep the same error type, so \u003Ccode>Bind\u003C/code> is a direct replacement.\u003C/p>\n",[6,10,13,16,19,22,25,28],{"id":7,"text":8,"level":9},"rules","Rules",2,{"id":11,"text":12,"level":9},"explicit-result-construction","Explicit Result Construction",{"id":14,"text":15,"level":9},"mapping-to-nullable-values","Mapping to Nullable Values",{"id":17,"text":18,"level":9},"safe-exception-adapters","Safe Exception Adapters",{"id":20,"text":21,"level":9},"cancellation-aware-tryasync","Cancellation-Aware TryAsync",{"id":23,"text":24,"level":9},"discarded-results-in-tap","Discarded Results in Tap",{"id":26,"text":27,"level":9},"discarded-results","Discarded Results",{"id":29,"text":30,"level":9},"failures-passed-on-by-hand","Failures Passed On by Hand","docs/analyzers.md"],"uses":{"params":["page","product"]}}]}
